#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0128 expect=violation domain=DM
#note "Authority: SDTM and SDTMIG Conformance Rules v2.0 CG0128 (SDTMIG 3.2), Condition \"ARMCD not in TA.ARMCD\", Rule \"ARMCD in (SCRNFAIL, NOTASSGN)\". The Check compares upper(ARMCD) with the exemption literals: that case-folding is the RULED idiom (PLAN-port-core-expression-improvements Q1(a), owner 2026-09-22; applied to this rule by CHANGE-arm-upper-alignment.tsv), not a Partially Executable limitation. The limitation is multi-stage Arm allocation (SDTMIG 3.2 DM Assumption 4, cited in rules-src/docs/CDISC/CDISC-CG0128.yaml): a subject who drops out between two allocation processes carries an ARMCD reflecting only the allocations undergone, which need not be a TA arm, and the Check would flag it. This fixture models a single-stage study (one allocation, every arm fully defined in TA), so that clause never arises. Row 2: ARMCD=XANLO is not a TA arm -> fires. Row 4: ARMCD=NOTTRT is not a TA arm and NOTTRT is NOT one of CG0128's two exemptions (it is a CG0124 ACTARMCD exemption only) -> fires. Rows 1 (PBO) and 3 (SCRNFAIL) silent. This S2 is also the S3 foreign discriminator (SKELETON-distinct-function hazard 3): a port reading ARMCD from DM instead of TA would put each row's own ARMCD in the set and never fire."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-2
#expectViolationCount 2
#expectViolationAt row=2 USUBJID=01-002 ARMCD=XANLO
#expectViolationAt row=4 USUBJID=01-004 ARMCD=NOTTRT
dataset DM label="Demographics"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col ARMCD    type=Char label="Planned Arm Code"
col ARM      type=Char label="Description of Planned Arm"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-001 | PBO      | Placebo
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-002 | XANLO    | Xanomeline Low
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-003 | SCRNFAIL | Screen Failure
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-004 | NOTTRT   | Not Treated
---

dataset TA label="Trial Arms"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col ARMCD   type=Char label="Planned Arm Code"
col ARM     type=Char label="Description of Planned Arm"
col TAETORD type=Num  label="Planned Order of Element within Arm"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col ELEMENT type=Char label="Description of Element"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | TA | PBO   | Placebo         | 1 | SCRN | Screening
CDISCPILOT01 | TA | PBO   | Placebo         | 2 | PBO  | Placebo
CDISCPILOT01 | TA | XANHI | Xanomeline High | 1 | SCRN | Screening
CDISCPILOT01 | TA | XANHI | Xanomeline High | 2 | XANH | Xanomeline High
---
